[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      114[0m:[38;5;10m[49m it sometimes landed on the write end of the pipe belonging to the broken-pipe
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      115[0m:[38;5;10m[49m test, which then saw a healthy pipe instead of a broken one.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      116[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      117[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Fixed by passing `Stdio::from(File)` and letting `spawn` close the parent's
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      118[0m:[38;5;10m[49m descriptor, with no manual `close`. Ten consecutive full runs of the suite now
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      119[0m:[38;5;10m[49m pass, 30 tests each.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      120[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      121[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The lesson generalises: a test that manipulates raw descriptors has to respect
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      122[0m:[38;5;10m[49m single ownership, or it will report mismatches that the program under test never
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      123[0m:[38;5;10m[49m committed.
