[1mTwo real mismatches found and fixed in the Rust program:[22m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
1. [1mExit status on a broken stdout pipe.[22m C exited 141, Rust exited 0. The Rust runtime sets [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m to [38;5;10mSIG_IGN[0m before [38;5;10mmain[0m runs; a C program inherits the default. So a failing write killed the C program with signal 13, while Rust merely got [38;5;10mEPIPE[0m, discarded it (correctly mirroring C's habit of ignoring [38;5;10mprintf[0m's return value), and fell through to [38;5;10mexit(0)[0m. Fixed by restoring [38;5;10mSIG_DFL[0m for [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m as the first statement of [38;5;10mmain[0m. Both binaries now report [38;5;10mreturncode=-13[0m when the reader is confirmed dead before launch.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
2. [1mBuffering discipline.[22m Not a byte difference, but a timing one. The translation wrote through [38;5;10mstd::io::stdout()[0m, a [38;5;10mLineWriter[0m regardless of destination — seven writes, the first almost immediately. C stdio picks its mode from the descriptor: line-buffered on a tty, fully buffered otherwise, so against a pipe C emitted all 92 bytes in a single exit-time flush. Running [38;5;10mprog | true[0m twenty times, failures were [1mone-directional[22m (C 141, Rust 0, never the reverse) — the signature of a systematic difference. [38;5;10mprint_line[0m now buffers and flushes the way C stdio does, writing straight to fd 1 in one call. Divergences became symmetric in both directions, which is the inherent race between two separately launched processes; the deterministic form agrees every run and is what the suite asserts.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mOne bug was in my own test harness, not the translation.[22m The broken-pipe test failed only under the full parallel suite. The pty test transferred a descriptor with [38;5;10mStdio::from_raw_fd[0m and then called [38;5;10mclose()[0m on the same number by hand — a double close that, across parallel test threads, sometimes shut the [3mother[23m test's pipe. Fixed by respecting single ownership. Ten consecutive full runs now pass.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The C program branches on nothing external: [38;5;10margc[0m/[38;5;10margv[0m are unused, stdin is never read, and the only conditional ([38;5;10mline != NULL[0m) is unreachable since every call site passes a literal. So the 30 tests concentrate on where branches actually exist — argv shape (2000 args, 64 KiB arg, non-UTF-8 bytes, empty string), stdin shape (1 MiB unread, all 256 byte values, closed fd 0), locale, and stdout state (dead pipe, [38;5;10m/dev/full[0m ENOSPC, closed fd 1 EBADF, regular file, pty, merged streams). Every case asserts all three of stdout, stderr and exit status, including terminating signal. [38;5;10mERRORS.md[0m records both mismatches, the harness defect, and the checks that found nothing — the last so a future reader knows they were exercised rather than assumed.[0m[0m
